  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The current best is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688 accuracy. The image modality contributed ~3.5% over RNA-only (0.653), suggesting the fusion mechanism is a critical lever. Config_033 is a single-variable change from the current best (concat → weighted fusion), directly testing whether learned fusion weights can better balance the strong RNA signal against the weaker image signal. This is the cleanest next comparison: if weighted fusion outperforms concat, we get a new best to build on in the remaining 2 experiments (e.g., pairing with ViT-L); if it underperforms, we confirm concat is optimal and can redirect remaining budget toward testing a stronger image encoder (ViT-L). This isolates one design choice without confounding, making it the highest-information experiment under the tight budget."
}

